  "overview": "**Radix** is a dark-first design system anchored on `#111111` canvas surfaces with `#f7f7f8` primary ink (17.6:1 contrast) and `#ffc53d` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `System UI` (16px display down to 16px body), unified by `6px` base corner radius and stepped `#111111` -> `#141110` surface layering.\n\nMaintained by **WorkOS**. Source: published token package, repo https://github.com/radix-ui/primitives, package `@radix-ui/colors`, frameworks: react, css. Inventory: **91** colors, **4** typography steps, and **16** documented components (MIT license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 16 component tokens with documented paddings: `10px 18px`, `9px 13px`, `18px 20px`, `4px 10px`, `10px 16px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#141110` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #f7f7f8 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`#111111` -> `#141110`) and `1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #f7f7f8 14%, transparent)` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#ffc53d` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#111111` (dark) with `#f7f7f8` primary text and `#f7f7f8` secondary labels.\n- Use `#ffc53d` with `#0b0b0c` text (12.5:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `System UI` headings with `System UI` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `6px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (10px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#141110` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #f7f7f8 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of dark polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `6px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input-default` fields and secondary buttons."
